Replaced the linear scan with a lazily built direct-mapped table from message number to the first matching `MESG` pointer, making lookups O(1) and invalid numbers return `NULL` immediately.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* lookup[65536];
    static bool initialized = false;
    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = static_cast<int>(MESGS) - 1; i >= 0; --i)
            lookup[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        initialized = true;
    }

    return lookup[num];
}
```